    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0365" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11 W 892/48</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Nelson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I respectfully beg leave
                    to call your attention to the enclosed bill, S. 3852,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d206-f1"/> (by Mr. Underwood) ‘to amend an Act entitled “An Act to
                    define, regulate, and punish trading with the enemy, and for other purposes,”
                    approved October 6, 1917, as amended,’ and to request that you furnish me, as
                    soon <pb facs="0366" n="252" xml:id="pg252"/> as may be, for the use of this
                    Committee, with your views, favorable or otherwise, as to the advisability of
                    the legislation proposed in this measure.</p>
                <p>Yours truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knute Nelson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
